IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cca-acl-mergers`

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth), Sch 2 ss 3, 18, 23-27, 50, 54, 64, 64A, 259-263, ss 131A and Part IVA -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_competition-and-consumer-act-2010.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*): Chloe, 29, has a new laptop fail in month three and
-- the retailer repairs it on 20 May 2032 (c070). Jake, 30, has debts of $41,000 and collectors call on 6 February 2037 (k064);
-- he took two credit cards on 2 March 2031 (k048). Daniel's company Jarrah, registered in March 2031 with three employees from
-- June, reviews its standard software terms with a liability cap on 10 July 2031 (d045); a competitor trades as JARRA on 11
-- February 2039 (d056); Jarrah acquires Formly Pty Ltd, "a smaller company", on 15 June 2043 (d065).
-- The scenarios give no laptop price, no subscription price, no customer, no turnover for Formly or Jarrah in 2043, and no
-- account of what the collectors did; the figures and flags used for them below are the encoder's, and each evaluative
-- judgement (acceptable quality, major failure, unfair, misleading, undue harassment) is set by hand, not decided by the Act.

